Package: llmClassificR
Title: Text Classification with Large Language Models
Version: 0.2.4
Authors@R: 
    person("Hudson", "Golino", , "hfg9s@virginia.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1601-1447"))
Description: A toolkit for text classification with large language models
    (LLMs), from bag-of-words baselines to general-purpose classification
    models. Provides batch zero-shot classification with LLMs served by
    'Groq' (direct, few-shot, chain-of-thought, JSON, strict JSON Schema,
    multi-model ensemble, self-consistency, scoring, and LLM-as-judge),
    classification with the 'Jev' model of 'TypeSafe' from pure R, embedding
    extraction through the 'Voyage AI' and 'Jina AI' services and from local
    'Hugging Face' transformer models, a do-it-yourself 'Jev'-like classifier
    built from label descriptions, calibration tools (expected calibration
    error, Brier score, reliability diagrams, temperature and Platt scaling),
    bag-of-words baselines, learning curves and linear probes,
    retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), synthetic data generation and
    quality checks, and unsupervised text classification with Exploratory
    Graph Analysis (EGA; Golino and Epskamp, 2017,
    <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0174035>), including a prime-weight encoding
    of the networks estimated from every layer of a transformer.
License: GPL (>= 3)
SystemRequirements: Python 3 and the uv package manager
    (optional; needed only for local transformer models and the Python
    clients of some services, see setup_llm_env())
